.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_OPEN_MPQE_IO 3 2026-09-24 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_open_mpqe_io \- open an MPQE-wrapped MPQ through random-access I/O.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_open_mpqe_io("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s **" "mpq_archive,"
.BI "        void            *" "context,"
.BI "        libmpq_read_at_fn " "read_at,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t    " "source_size,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t    " "archive_offset,"
.BI "        const uint8_t    *" "auth_code,"
.BI "        size_t            " "auth_code_size,"
.BI "        const char       *" "source_name"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open an MPQE transport stream through the same borrowed exact random-access
callback contract as \fBlibmpq__archive_open_io\fP(). libmpq obtains encrypted
bytes through the callback, applies its MPQE transform, and parses the result
as an MPQ. The context remains caller-owned through every related clone.
.PP
\fIsource_name\fP follows the same optional copied logical-name rules as
\fBlibmpq__archive_open_io\fP(), including basename-dependent legacy strong
signature verification.
.PP
At least 32 authentication-code bytes are required. An incorrect code is not
identifiable by MPQE alone and can therefore produce an ordinary MPQ parser
error after decryption.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, *\fImpq_archive\fP receives a new \fBmpq_archive_s\fP and zero is
returned. On failure, the output handle is NULL. The errors documented for
\fBlibmpq__archive_open_io\fP can apply. \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_DECRYPT\fP reports a
NULL or too-short authentication code.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__archive_open_io (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_clone (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_close (3)
